Several questions remain. One is to characterize the instances on which SPSE is automatically score-feasible; by Remark~\ref{rem:overlap-cause} such a characterization must rule out two independent causes at once. A second is whether the incentive loss of Proposition~\ref{prop:paodr-notsp} is unavoidable: is there any score-feasible strategy-proof mechanism here, necessarily de-reserving, and at what cost in reserve capacity? A third is the complexity of \textsc{MinDeres} for unbounded $|T|$; we conjecture hardness, since realizability rests on a Hall-type condition over all subsets of $T$. A fourth is to compare PA-ODR with the idle-seat variant of Remark~\ref{sec:trigger} on the dimensions a policymaker weighs, reserve seats retained against students matched. Finally, the common bonus $k$ is deliberate: category-specific bonuses would break the property that an overlapping student is admissible for all her categories or none, which is what keeps the feasibility graph simple here.

